# Access Denial Script Example

Here's a simple web server script that denies access to a website or service. I'll provide examples in different languages and contexts.

## 1. Node.js/Express Middleware (JavaScript)
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

// Middleware to deny all access
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.status(403).send(`
    <html>
      <head><title>Access Denied</title></head>
      <body>
        <h1>403 Forbidden</h1>
        <p>Access to this website has been restricted.</p>
      </body>
    </html>
  `);
});

const PORT = 3000;
app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running. All access denied on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

## 2. Python Flask Example
```python
from flask import Flask, abort

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.before_request
def deny_all():
    abort(403, description="Access to this service has been restricted.")

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(port=5000)
```

## 3. Nginx Configuration (Deny All Access)
```nginx
server {
    listen 80;

    location / {
        return 403;
        # Or for a custom denial page
        # root /path/to/error/pages;
        # error_page 403 /403.html;
        # return 403;
    }
}
```

## 4. Apache .htaccess Example
```apache
Order deny,allow
Deny from all
```

## 5. Windows Batch Script to Block Website via Hosts File
```batch
@echo off
:: Requires Administrator privileges
echo 127.0.0.1 example.com >> C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts
ipconfig /flushdns
echo Access to example.com has been denied
pause
```

## 6. PHP Denial Script (for existing websites)
```php
<?php
header('HTTP/1.0 403 Forbidden');
die('<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Access Denied</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>403 Forbidden</h1>
    <p>You are not authorized to access this resource.</p>
</body>
</html>');
```

## Advanced: IP-based Denial (Node.js Example)
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

// Array of banned IPs
const BANNED_IPS = ['192.168.1.100', '10.0.0.5'];

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const ip = req.ip || req.connection.remoteAddress;

  if (BANNED_IPS.includes(ip)) {
    return res.status(403).send('Access denied - your IP has been blocked.');
  }

  next();
});

// Allow other routes
app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  res.send('Welcome to the site');
});

app.listen(3000);
```

Choose the method that best fits your environment. The implementation will depend on where you want to block access - at the server level (Nginx/Apache), application level (Node/Python/PHP), or host level (hosts file).
